  I *like* the idea of trading bones files!  Splendid!  I just wish I had one
  to trade, which is the purpose of this post...

  First, a bit of bragging (it does fit in with my problem, honest!):
  For the first time, I finished NetHack 3.0.10!  I was playing a Valkyrie
  who, when ascending, was at level 20 with AC -23 and 191 HP.  Items of in-
  terest:  blessed +3 Stormbringer, No enchantment gray dragon SM, +2 gauntlets
  of power, -1 helm of telepathy (bad time with a golden naga), and +7 in rings
  of protection.  Everything else was pretty run-o'-the-mill.  My score was
  about a million and a half (I was playing to finish, not to get a high
  score).

  Now, the meat of the post:  This was the PC version of NetHack.  When I
  started the game, I had three bones levels in my bones directory and during
  the game I encountred none of them (no shops, either, come to think of it).
  But when I finished the game and went to check the directory (because the
  game had filled the hardrive with temp files for the hell levels at one point
  and I was curious if the files were still there) I found the game had cleaned
  up after itself too well.  *Everything* in the directory was gone:  Bones and
  temp files alike.

  So, my questions:  (1) Is this a bug or is it intentional?  (2) Does this
  mean you cannot have more than one game saved at a time (ie: If you finish
  the game you had been playing using a tourist, will your save file for your
  rogue be lost when the game cleans up)?  (3) Or, to put 2 more completely,
  can multiple saved games on PC NetHack corrupt one another?   

  Thanks.
